  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill, so `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow` applies. After the front matter it has the title `# Habeas requirements` and a short two-sentence preamble. The first `##` section is `## Workflow`, which holds the numbered steps 1–7, each written as a checklist item (`- [ ] 1.` through `- [ ] 7.`). The later sections are `## Writing chapters`, `## Choosing references`, `## What the review checks` and `## Gotchas`. All of them come after the workflow. The preamble belongs to the title section and is not a separate section, so the workflow still opens the skill before any other section. The steps are numbered and in order, so they meet the \"ordered steps\" obligation. There are no violation matches to assess, and I found no gap.",
